Compound Interest Calculator in C
About the Project

This is a simple Compound Interest Calculator developed using the C programming language.
The program takes the principal amount, annual interest rate, number of times interest is compounded per year, and time period as input from the user.
It calculates the final amount and compound interest.

Concepts Learned

Through this project, I practised the following C programming concepts:

Variables: Declaring variables using double and int.
Constants: Using const for fixed values.
User Input: Using scanf() to get input from the user.
Output: Using printf() to display results.
Mathematical Operations: Performing multiplication, division, and subtraction.
Math Library: Using math.h and the pow() function.
Format Specifiers: Using %lf and %.2lf.
Formulas: Applying mathematical formulas in C.

Formula Used

Compound Interest Formula:

A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt)

Compound Interest:

CI = A - P

Where:
P = Principal amount
r = Annual interest rate (in decimal)
n = Number of times interest is compounded per year
t = Time period in years
A = Final amount
CI = Compound interest

How the Program Works
The program asks the user to enter the principal amount.
It asks for the annual interest rate.
It asks how many times the interest is compounded per year.
It asks for the time period in years.
It calculates the final amount using the compound interest formula.
Finally, it displays the total amount and compound interest.

What I Learned
This project helped me understand how to apply mathematical formulas in C, use the pow() function, work with floating-point values, take multiple inputs, and perform financial calculations.
